From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LuneOS / webOS Ports <team@webos-ports.org>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Makefile.common: do not force -O0 -Werror

The Makefile appends its own flags after the ones the build system passes, so
-O0 overrides the distro's -O2 while -D_FORTIFY_SOURCE=2 stays. glibc then
refuses the combination, and the hardcoded -Werror makes it fatal:

  features.h:451:4: error: #warning _FORTIFY_SOURCE requires compiling with
  optimization (-O) [-Werror=cpp]

Overriding CFLAGS from the command line is not an option here because the same
variable carries -DPURPLE_PLUGINS and -DMATRIX_NO_E2E. Drop -O0 so the distro
decides the optimization level, and drop -Werror, which has no place in a
distribution build where compiler versions vary.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 Makefile.common | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Makefile.common b/Makefile.common
index c800bd1..4c77fb5 100644
--- a/Makefile.common
+++ b/Makefile.common
@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@
 
 COMPILE.c = $(CC) $(CFLAGS) $(CPPFLAGS) $(TARGET_ARCH) -c
 
-CFLAGS+=-Wall -g -O0 -Werror
+CFLAGS+=-Wall -g
 CFLAGS += -DPURPLE_PLUGINS 
 CFLAGS += -DGLIB_DISABLE_DEPRECATION_WARNINGS
 
